diagnosis_text:
Affected component: The access interface toward pc_0_0 on leaf_router_0_0 (interface eth2, gateway IP 10.0.0.1) is administratively down.

Mechanism: With the leaf access port down, pc_0_0 cannot ARP its default gateway (10.0.0.1). This causes local delivery failures before any traffic reaches the fabric, producing “Destination Host Unreachable” from 10.0.0.2 and an ARP entry “10.0.0.1 dev eth0 FAILED.” Because the failure is on the leaf-port, not the fabric, nothing traverses to the spines.

Localization and evidence:
- pc_0_0: default via 10.0.0.1; ping 10.0.0.1 returns Destination Host Unreachable; ip neigh shows 10.0.0.1 FAILED; ethtool eth0 reports link detected: yes.
- leaf_router_0_0: eth2 (10.0.0.1/2
