is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_0
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: The access interface toward pc_0_0 on leaf_router_0_0 (interface eth2, gateway IP 10.0.0.1) is administratively down.

Mechanism: With the leaf access port down, pc_0_0 cannot ARP its default gateway (10.0.0.1). This causes local delivery failures before any traffic reaches the fabric, producing “Destination Host Unreachable” from 10.0.0.2 and an ARP entry “10.0.0.1 dev eth0 FAILED.” Because the failure is on the leaf-port, not the fabric, nothing traverses to the spines.

Localization and evidence:
- pc_0_0: default via 10.0.0.1; ping 10.0.0.1 returns Destination Host Unreachable; ip neigh shows 10.0.0.1 FAILED; ethtool eth0 reports link detected: yes.
- leaf_router_0_0: eth2 (10.0.0.1/24) is DOWN (ip -br link shows DOWN; ethtool “Link detected: no”); no RX/TX on eth2. Uplinks eth0/eth1 are UP, and BGP to both spines is Established with prefixes exchanged, proving the fabric and spine_router_0_0 are healthy.

Root cause: The leaf access interface leaf_router_0_0:eth2 was administratively shut/left down, severing connectivity for pc_0_0.

Corrective fix: Bring the interface back up on leaf_router_0_0. Example: “ip link set dev eth2 up” (or restart the leaf’s network service to reapply intent). Verify ARP to 10.0.0.1 on pc_0_0 then end-to-end ping to 10.0.1.2. No spine replacement is required; the fabric is functioning correctly.
=== END ===